{title:Title}

{p 8 17 2}
{bf:pythonedu} -- Python beginner's learning program: installation and basics

{title:Syntax}

{p 8 13 2}
{cmd:pythonedu} [{cmd:install} {cmd:basic} {cmd:example} {cmd:all}]

{title:Description}

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:pythonedu} is an entry-level learning program for Python beginners,
published by Dingyuan Accounting, which follows the academic principle of
{bf:scientific and standardized, humane and good}. In three short lessons
it helps you get to know Python quickly: installing Anaconda, the basic
syntax, and a complete data-analysis example.

{p 4 4 2}
With no options, {cmd:pythonedu} displays all three lessons in turn. Use the
options to review a single lesson at any time.

{title:Options}

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:install} displays only lesson 1: how to download, install, and verify Anaconda.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:basic} displays only lesson 2: print(), variables, data types, lists, dictionaries, loops, and pandas.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:example} displays only lesson 3: a complete, ready-to-run ROE analysis example.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:all} displays all three lessons (the default).

{title:Examples}

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:. pythonedu}

{p 4 4 2}
Displays all three lessons.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:. pythonedu, basic}

{p 4 4 2}
Displays only the Python basics.

{p 4 4 2}
{cmd:. pythonedu, example}

{p 4 4 2}
Displays only the ROE analysis example.

{title:Remarks}

{p 4 4 2}
{bf:Learning tips}

{p 4 8 2}
1. Run {cmd:pythonedu} and read all three lessons first.

{p 4 8 2}
2. Open Spyder, paste the whole example from lesson 3 into a new file, and press Run (F5).

{p 4 8 2}
3. Do not fear errors: reading error messages is the most important Python lesson.

{p 4 8 2}
4. Be persistent: 30 minutes a day and you will be a Python beginner in one week.

{p 4 4 2}
{bf:Dingyuan Accounting} adheres to the principle of
{bf:scientific and standardized, humane and good} and hopes every beginner
learns with joy.

